# Nine constant characters are two stores of immediates: eight bytes (0x64742f3c3e64743c, "<td></td" from the lowest byte up) and one. The cursor goes up by nine.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="row" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[limit]] = Phi(
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[cursor]] = Phi(
# CHECK: Store($7238462436882543676(b@{{*}}), b@[[cursor]], ControlDependent|Writes:stringBuilderBytes, {{*}}:StringBuilderAppendConstant)
# CHECK: Store8($62(b@{{*}}), b@[[cursor]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Writes:stringBuilderBytes, {{*}}:StringBuilderAppendConstant)
# CHECK-NOT: Load(
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[next]] = Add(b@[[cursor]], $9(
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[fits]] = BelowEqual(b@[[next]], b@[[limit]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[fits]], Terminal,
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# There is one loop. Nothing is called in it but the poll and, in the rare block for a full buffer, the stub that makes room, behind which the limit is read again. No cell is made or loaded for the literal, and its characters are not read from memory.
# HOT-LABEL: name="row" role=Source
# HOT-NOT: Reads:characters
# HOT-NOT: Reads:AOTInstance
# HOT-NOT: :String)
# HOT-NOT: Patchpoint(
# HOT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#[[full]]
# HOT-NOT: Patchpoint(
# HOT: Void b@{{*}} = Patchpoint({{*}}isLoopPoll
# HOT-NOT: Patchpoint(
# HOT: BB#[[full]]:
# HOT: = Patchpoint(
# HOT-NEXT: Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:AOTStackStringBuilder_fields,
# HOT-NEXT: Upsilon(
# HOT-NEXT: Upsilon(
# HOT-NEXT: Jump(
# HOT: end of loop
# HOT-NOT: loop #
# HOT-LABEL: end of function
# The loop holds a poll, so x86-64 is counted where the calling convention is not that of Windows.
# X64-LABEL: name="row" role=Source
# X64-NEXT: instructions: 6, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 3
# ARM64-LABEL: name="row" role=Source
